      "text": "To solve for the two positive real numbers, let's denote them as \\(a\\) and \\(b\\). We are given the following conditions:\n\n1. The geometric mean of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is \\(\\sqrt{3}\\).\n2. The harmonic mean of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is \\(\\frac{3}{2}\\).\n\nThe geometric mean of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is given by:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{ab} = \\sqrt{3}\n\\]\nSquaring both sides, we get:\n\\[\nab = 3\n\\]\n\nThe harmonic mean of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is given by:\n\\[\n\\frac{2ab}{a + b} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\nSubstituting \\(ab = 3\\) into the harmonic mean formula, we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{2 \\cdot 3}{a + b} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\nSimplifying the left side, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{6}{a + b} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\nCross-multiplying to solve for \\(a + b\\), we get:\n\\[\n6 \\cdot 2 = 3 \\cdot (a + b)\n\\]\n\\[\n12 = 3(a + b)\n\\]\n\\[\na + b = 4\n\\]\n\nNow we have a system of equations:\n1. \\(ab = 3\\)\n2. \\(a + b = 4\\)\n\nThese equations represent a quadratic equation whose roots are \\(a\\) and \\(b\\). The quadratic equation can be written as:\n\\[\nx^2 - (a+b)x + ab = 0\n\\]\nSubstituting the known values, we get:\n\\[\nx^2 - 4x + 3 = 0\n\\]\nWe solve this quadratic equation using the factoring method:\n\\[\nx^2 - 4x + 3 = (x-1)(x-3) = 0\n\\]\nSo, the solutions are:\n\\[\nx = 1 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x = 3\n\\]\nTherefore, the two numbers are \\(1\\) and \\(3\\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1, 3}\n\\]",
